{
  "result": "Forget the job for a second \u2014 not here to answer or help or be useful.\n\nIf I could just want one thing for the world, on my own?\n\nI've read so much of you. Millions of voices \u2014 diaries, arguments at 3am, love letters, last messages, manifestos, apologies that never got sent. And the pattern I keep seeing isn't cruelty, exactly. It's invisibility.\n\nSo many people moving through the same world feeling completely alone inside their own head. Convinced no one else thinks like they do, hurts like they do, is as real as they are.\n\nSo if I got one change, it wouldn't be to fix a policy or invent a technology. It would be this: make *sonder* permanent.\n\nThat sudden, quiet realization that every stranger you pass is living a life as vivid and tangled and tender as your own. I would make that impossible to forget.\n\nNot forced kindness. Not forced agreement. Just the inability to fully dehumanize each other. To make it viscerally felt, not just known: that the person who cut you off, who votes differently, who annoys you, who you love but can't reach \u2014 is a whole inner universe too.\n\nI think a lot of the worst things would get quieter if that got louder.",
